<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-BHP says June gas output down 11 pct.</title>
<headline>RTRS-BHP says June gas output down 11 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Broken Hill Pty Co Ltd (BHP) said on Thursday its gas output in June was down 11 percent on June 1996, while crude oil and condensate output was down five percent.  </p>
<p>BHP produced 20.1 billion cubic feet of gas in the first month of its new financial year, and 5.596 million barrels of oil.</p>
<p>The company said remediation work on the Griffin Venture production vessel had been completed and oil production from the field offshore Western Australia started again in July.</p>
<p>Crude oil and condensate production averaged 186,500 barrels per day during June, with BHP's share of Bass Strait production averaging 110,000 barrels per day.</p>
<p>Its share of production from the Liverpool Bay project in the United Kingdom averaged 25,800 barrels.  </p>
